{
  "text": " So we ask that you join us. DC isn't that far away and January 3rd is not far away. 23rd, on January 23rd we're coming together, black, white and Hispanic, vaccinated and unvaccinated, Democrats and Republicans, for freedom to march on Washington in peace. The discrimination against the unvaccinated is an assault against the very fabric of what makes a free Democratic society. Europe and Australia and countries around the world have risen up in massive protests in which hundreds of thousands of people have come together. The worldwide rally for freedom has protested vaccine mandates and passports. January 23rd will be the next day that the whole world comes together. It's time for America to step up and join the worldwide rally for freedom. The plan currently is to walk together from Washington Monument to the Lincoln Memorial where there will be a program of featured speakers, Peters among them, as is Bobby Kennedy, as is myself. The first half will consist of thought leaders and medical experts. The second half would highlight several national celebrities who will make a stand against the mandates. The ask for everyone at the march is very simple. Do not comply. Ultimately, our hope is that the defeat the mandates in American homecoming rally will help bring about new policies at the federal, state and city level to eliminate the blatant discrimination that's happening in front of our eyes. We are not against the vaccinated. Again, we are not against the vaccinated. We are against forcing vaccinations on Americans and on the world. It is time for America to stand up and time for America to come home. Sign up to join me at the march. You can find that at defeat the mandates DC dot com. Thank you for your time. I hope to see you in DC. Thank you.",
